From: t00mietum <73576036+t00mietum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:07:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wayfire: keep keyboard focus off context menus

Since Wayfire 0.9 an xdg-popup with a grab takes keyboard focus. Each
focus change sends the client a new selection offer, and Qt's context
menu "Paste" then reads the offer that was replaced a moment before. It
pastes nothing whenever the text was copied in another app. Ctrl+V is
not affected, which is what makes it look random.

Wayfire 0.10 added an opt-in workaround that leaves keyboard focus on
the main window. Turn it on for the LXQt session.

See https://github.com/WayfireWM/wayfire/issues/2600
---
 configurations/lxqt-wayfire.ini | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/configurations/lxqt-wayfire.ini b/configurations/lxqt-wayfire.ini
index 1d6aba0edcc9eb64123e1a3f59bb1fdacc7e915b..51b77f369ae79a28bf1fdbe70ad5eb405b40fbea 100644
--- a/configurations/lxqt-wayfire.ini
+++ b/configurations/lxqt-wayfire.ini
@@ -96,6 +96,11 @@ vheight = 3
 # Prefer client-side decoration or server-side decoration
 preferred_decoration_mode = server
 
+# Qt apps paste nothing from a context menu when the text was copied in another
+# app, if the menu takes keyboard focus. Wayfire 0.10 and later.
+[workarounds]
+focus_main_surface_instead_of_popup = true
+
 # Mouse bindings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 
 # Drag windows by holding down Super and left mouse button.
